grind text

// A text document written by hand — the starter `grind init --template text` writes.
//
// This file *is* the document, in the form that lives in git: one block per line, so a change
// is a line of diff. Open it in grind's window, or turn it into a file anybody opens:
//
//   grind lint     notes.grind              the problems, if it has any
//   grind convert  notes.grind notes.odt    a package for anybody else
//
// The guide is grind's doc/projection-text.md (https://github.com/fwilhe2/grind).

h 1 "Notes"
p "A paragraph is a `p`, and **bold** and *italic* are written the way you would type them."

h 2 "A list"
list {
    li "Each item is a line."
    li "An item inside a `list` takes its depth from the nesting:"
    list {
        li "like this one."
    }
}

h 2 "A table"
table "Costs" {
    row {
        cell { p "Item" }
        cell { p "Monthly" }
    }
    row {
        cell { p "Rent" }
        cell { p "1450" }
    }
}
